cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its accompanying technical note, please cite it as below."
title: "JAMO: Judging Accuracy of Machine-rendered Orthography"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Lim"
    given-names: "Taewoo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4014-384X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nasser-Lim/jamo-bench"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/Nasser4963/jamo-gold"
abstract: >-
  An OCR-mediated benchmark that diagnoses Hangul visual-text rendering at
  the jamo (onset/nucleus/coda) level. JAMO's central finding is that
  OCR-based judges systematically conceal Hangul rendering failures by
  snapping malformed or nonexistent glyphs to the nearest valid syllable,
  and it provides a confidence-gated judging protocol plus human-verified
  ground truth to measure and correct for that concealment.
keywords:
  - hangul
  - ocr
  - benchmark
  - text-to-image
  - measurement-validity
  - typography
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-17"
